r energy that it had  earlier on even the last person that  paul fights feels like a major step down  in terms of action as it's someone he  easily beats and it's not really a  character that feels like they should  have been the final battle in a movie  looking at the way they've adapted the  source material i think they've really  gone about it the wrong way and the  movie structure makes it feel like it  has a beginning middle and an end and  then a beginning in the middle following  on from it i'm gonna say something super  controversial here so hold on to your  butts but i actually think that a new  hope did a better job of adapting june  than june did now what i mean by that is  that a new hope introduces its  characters the threat we spend some time  on a planet face peril on the death star  and then have a big blowout against the  seemingly unbeatable enemy which wraps  up the movie juxtaposing this dune  introduces the characters the threat we  spend some time on a planet move there  lots of people die we stay there and  then it just kind of wind down introduce  new characters in the last 15 minutes  and then we end the movie it's a weird  way to tell the story and i think that  it does massively affect the pacing of  the film and in the end it just makes it  feel a bit bloated i was actually saying  to my friends i think it would have  worked better if they'd spent longer at  the front part of the movie and then  ended after the attack on the planet  with leno's death being what closed  things out books also don't have to be  adapted completely to remain faithful  either and i think that the movie could  have ended with paul and jessica meeting  the fremen robin showing up to get  revenge for his uncle and the final  showdown of the film being between the  fremen paul and rabban's forces this  would allow a big bad who's been laced  throughout the movie to make an impact  and it would also show the fremen that  paul wasn't messing around a new hope  kept the pace up by having us jump from  location to location from planet to  planet but here we're stuck in the sand  and though i know that's what happens in  the book it feels a bit stagnant  honestly it's kind of bloated and  there's also no real payoff knowing that  we are getting a sequel means that we  can kind of push these criticisms to the  side and be like well we will get  resolution but if warner brothers pull  the plug then i don't know if this movie  will feel like a smart move to lay this  story out the way that it did i'm not  going to score this film because hey i'm  a guy who gives something like halloween  kills a 10 out of 10 because i had fun  watching it objectively this is a better  movie than that but it's also just got a  feeling that it's not finished and thus  it's difficult to really rate it the  sequel might release and it could make  this movie much much better on  re-watches but on its own two feet i  don't feel like it's that strong that  being said it's expertly directed and i  think the best term for it is that it's  an epic space opera as a piece of art it  works incredibly well but as a movie  going experience i'm really mixed on it  i'm gonna rewatch it and obviously  people will take different things from  it and i'm hoping that down the line  that i appreciate the movie more if you  loved it then i'm glad that you enjoyed  it and if you disliked it then your  opinion is just as valid too obviously  let me know your thoughts below and if  you want something else to watch then  make sure you check out our halloween  kills breakdown so you can see why it's  the best movie of all time if not then  thanks for sitting until the end of the  video i've been paul you've been the  best and i'll see you on the next one  take care peace
 

